cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use BioKGSuite in your research, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >
  BioKGSuite: a multidimensional evaluation framework for biomedical
  knowledge graphs
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Molins
    given-names: Emily
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, University of Oxford; Ellison Institute of Technology"
  - family-names: Holmes
    given-names: Chris
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, University of Oxford; Ellison Institute of Technology"
  - family-names: Orfanoudaki
    given-names: Agni
    affiliation: "Saïd Business School, University of Oxford"
  - family-names: Ktena
    given-names: Ira
    affiliation: "Ellison Institute of Technology"
  - family-names: González
    given-names: Javier
    affiliation: "Ellison Institute of Technology"
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/emmolins/biokgsuite-bib"
url: "https://github.com/emmolins/biokgsuite-bib"
abstract: >
  BioKGSuite evaluates biomedical knowledge graphs across seven dimensions
  (coverage, annotation accuracy, trustworthiness, topology, stability, task
  performance and generalisation) through 19 metrics computed from each
  graph's released files and task-specific reference data. This release
  applies it to six knowledge graphs (Hetionet, DRKG, PrimeKG, BioKG,
  OpenBioLink and MATRIX) for drug repurposing, with reference data from
  MONDO, Open Targets and the Comparative Toxicogenomics Database, and
  includes a prospective experiment grounding large language models in
  evidence from three of the graphs.
keywords:
  - biomedical knowledge graph
  - drug repurposing
  - evaluation framework
  - PrimeKG
  - Hetionet
  - DRKG
  - OpenBioLink
  - BioKG
  - MATRIX
  - link prediction
  - computational biomedicine
